    description: "Forward slices stop at interface boundaries in DI-heavy Java codebases (Guice, CDI, SPI). This is the #1 gap identified in Java bakeoff assessments (keycloak: 62/100 refactoring, killbill: 30/100 refactoring, jenkins: 58/100 refactoring). Options: (a) Parse Guice module bindings (bind(X).to(Y)), (b) Detect CDI @Inject qualifiers, (c) Parse ServiceLoader patterns, (d) Heuristic: match interface method to Default* implementation. Source: bakeoff-features-reflect cohort keycloak/killbill/jenkins 2026-02-26."  # 4f9e
